{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 693 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Cytarabine has been on FDA's shortage list since 2021-09-24 and as of 2026-10-21 has remained listed for 61 months.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale General and Corvale East carries NDC 25021022320 and is labeled by Sagent Pharmaceuticals with manufacturing at a plant identified as GLAND.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E1", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "GLAND corresponds to Gland Pharma Limited (FEI 3009056604), which FDA inspected most recently on 2019-11-01 and classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2019-12-10 — 693 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2021-09-24.",
      "cites": ["E11", "E10", "D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier FDA inspections of the same plant in 2013-08-05 and 2015-06-30 were also classified VAI.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A more recent inspection of Gland Pharma Limited on 2023-07-28 was classified NAI.",
      "cites": ["E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 25 vials of the 100 mg/mL, 20 mL presentation at 2.9 vials per day, giving 8.7 days on hand, while Corvale General holds 67 vials at 2.7 vials per day, giving 24.5 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 16 vials of 100 mg/mL, 20 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would bring Corvale East to about 14 days on hand while Corvale General retains roughly two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    }
  ]
}
